Keep big-endian shared image surfaces in WebRender byte order.

The compositor shared-surface IPC path only accepts B8G8R8A8/B8G8R8X8 image
buffers. After preserving native Cairo formats on big-endian builds, vector/SVG
image rasterization can ask imgFrame to allocate explicit
A8R8G8B8/X8R8G8B8 shared surfaces. SourceSurfaceSharedData auto-shares those
buffers during Init(), so the content process can hit
SharedSurfacesChild::ShareInternal's release assert before the image is even
drawn.

Normalize image buffers backed by SourceSurfaceSharedData back to WebRender's
BGRA/BGRX byte layout at allocation time. DrawTargetCairo's SPARC data-target
bridge still lets Cairo draw through a native-endian temporary surface and
flushes back to this shared BGRA/BGRX buffer, so this keeps both sides of the
contract explicit.

Dependency: apply after SPARC-01-cairo-surface-format.patch and
SPARC-02-cairo-data-target.patch. The allocation format decision depends on the
base surface-format contract, and Cairo drawing into these shared buffers relies
on the data-target bridge.

--- firefox-153.0/image/imgFrame.cpp
+++ firefox-153.0/image/imgFrame.cpp
@@ -47,8 +47,25 @@ return SurfaceType::DATA_RECYCLING_SHARE
   }
 };
 
+static SurfaceFormat SharedImageSurfaceFormat(SurfaceFormat aFormat) {
+#if defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+  switch (aFormat) {
+    case SurfaceFormat::A8R8G8B8:
+      return SurfaceFormat::B8G8R8A8;
+    case SurfaceFormat::X8R8G8B8:
+      return SurfaceFormat::B8G8R8X8;
+    default:
+      return aFormat;
+  }
+#else
+  return aFormat;
+#endif
+}
+
